# Diagrams: the painter lays out every part. The brain names the shape and
# writes the parts; nothing here has a coordinate except the map's pins.

scene caption
flow plant right | Should I water this plant?
node start end | A drooping leaf
node dry ask from=start | Is the top inch of soil dry?
node water from=dry:yes fill=accent | Water it, slowly
node wait from=dry:no | Wait two days
node light from=wait | Check the light instead
say | Check the soil, not the calendar.
wait 1

# A follow-up continues the scene. Said again exactly as it stands, the flow and its steps cost nothing: no new element, no entrance.
# Only what is new lands, where it belongs.
flow plant right | Should I water this plant?
node dry ask from=start | Is the top inch of soil dry?
node pot from=light | Roots at the holes? Repot
say aside | One more step, and the rest has not moved.
wait 7s

scene caption
tree down | Where a sentence comes from
node root | Sentence
node subject from=root | Subject
node predicate from=root | Predicate
node noun from=subject | The cat
node verb from=predicate | sat on
node object from=predicate | the mat
say aside | Every sentence is a tree before it is a line.
wait 5.2s

scene caption
cycle | Water, always moving
node sea | Sea
node cloud | Cloud
node rain | Rain
node river | River
link rain river | runs off
say | Nothing is used up. It only changes where it is.
wait 4.5s

scene caption
timeline | The way to the Moon
node 1957 | Sputnik
node 1961 | First human in orbit
node 1969 | Apollo 11
node 1961 1972 note | The Apollo programme
say aside | Twelve years from the first satellite to the first footprint.
wait 5.4s

